<section class="blk blk--cream2">
  <p class="eyebrow">The question</p>
  <h2 class="sec">What does one human actually need?</h2>
  <p class="lead">Instead of starting from ideology, Uncost starts from the physical and social basics of a dignified life — fifteen sectors, from Food and Shelter to Communication and Leisure. Every part of the essential basket maps to one of them.</p>
  <p>Costs are local, so we measure and label them by region rather than pretending a single national number tells the whole story — and we say plainly how much of the country a figure covers.</p>
